    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43692" root="&#xA;                        ملك&#xA;                    " body-key="m1">
                        
                            2
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَلَّكَهُ</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>He made him to possess</i> a thing;
(S, K;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَمْلَكَهُ</span></b> . (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>He made him
king;</i> or <i>made him to have dominion, kingship,</i>
or <i>rule.</i> (Msb, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يُمَلَّكَ الرَّجُلُ أَمْرَهُ</span> [<i>The
man shall be made to have the ruling,</i> or <i>ordering,
of his affair,</i> or <i>affairs,</i> or <i>case</i>]. (Sh, T in art.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دين</span>.)

